BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-domain-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205350Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: .ART Award 2026 (Global Art Prize)
DESCRIPTION:Global art prize celebrating how art is made\, open to artists 
 worldwide working in any medium or art form. Instead of a traditional appl
 ication form\, artists submit a digital presence (website\, portfolio or s
 ocial profile) linked through a .ART domain that documents identity\, proc
 ess and work as one continuous record. PRIZES: Grand Prize (USD 15\,000 ca
 sh)\; Artist Residency Award France (one month at Chateau du Fresne\, near
  Paris)\; Artist Residency Award Spain (residency at Anfitrion\, Marbella)
 \; Publication Award (editorial coverage in Whitewall Magazine\, the campa
 ign's media partner)\; .ART Domain Award (USD 10\,000 premium .ART domain 
 name). ELIGIBILITY: individual artists and artist collectives from all bac
 kgrounds (cultures\, ethnicities\, gender identities\, abilities)\; 18 or 
 older at time of submission\; open to artists from all geographic regions 
 with no restrictions on nationality or place of residence. Multiple entrie
 s permitted\, as long as each submission (single artwork\, series or overa
 ll practice) is presented on or linked to a SEPARATE .ART domain. NOTE: a 
 .ART domain is required for submission\; this is the de facto entry mechan
 ism. ANNOUNCEMENT: winners revealed during Art Basel Miami on 3 December 2
 026. DEADLINE: 1 November 2026. APPLY via the .ART Award site.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: .ART (with Whitewall Magazine\, Chateau du Fresne\, Anfitrion)\nLoca
 tion: Hybrid mobility (Grand Prize cash + residencies in France and Spain)
 \nAward: More than USD 50\,000 in total prizes. Grand Prize: USD 15\,000 c
 ash. Artist Residency Award (France): one month at Chateau du Fresne\, nea
 r Paris. Artist Residency Award (Spain): residency at Anfitrion in Marbell
 a. Publication Award: editorial coverage in Whitewall Magazine (campaign m
 edia partner). .ART Domain Award: a USD 10\,000 premium .ART domain name. 
 No application fee mentioned (submission is via a .ART domain that documen
 ts the practice).\nDuration: One-off open call\; winners revealed during A
 rt Basel Miami on 3 December 2026\; residency prizes scheduled separately\
 n\nMore: https://www.award.art/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://www.award.art/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Hybrid mobility (Grand Prize cash + residencies in France and Spai
 n)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lee-ufan-arles-art-environment-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205350Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Lee Ufan Arles: Prix Art & Environnement 2026 (Residency 
 + Exhibition Prize)
DESCRIPTION:The Prix Art & Environnement (4th edition)\, awarded by Lee Ufa
 n Arles and Maison Guerlain\, supports an artist working at the intersecti
 on of art and the natural environment. The prize winner receives a funded 
 6–8 week production residency in Arles in early 2027\, including product
 ion space\, accommodation\, and mentorship from Lee Ufan Arles staff\, cul
 minating in a solo summer 2027 exhibition. ELIGIBILITY: open to all artist
 s of any discipline and nationality\, with no age or degree requirements\;
  candidates must demonstrate at least one solo exhibition and one or more 
 group exhibitions. DEADLINE: 31 July 2026. APPLY via the Google Form linke
 d from the Lee Ufan Arles website.\n\nOrganisation: Lee Ufan Arles and Mai
 son Guerlain\nLocation: Arles\, France (residency and exhibition)\nAward: 
 Funded residency (production space + accommodation) in Arles. No cash priz
 e amount specified. No application fee.\nDuration: 6–8 weeks residency i
 n early 2027\, followed by a solo summer 2027 exhibition\n\nMore: https://
 en.leeufan-arles.org/evenements/art-environment-prize?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://en.leeufan-arles.org/evenements/art-environment-prize?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Arles\, France (residency and exhibition)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:future-vision-xprize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205350Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Future Vision XPRIZE (sci-fi film competition)
DESCRIPTION:Future Vision XPRIZE is a sci-fi film competition challenging f
 ilmmakers to portray an optimistic\, abundant future for humanity rather t
 han a dystopian one. CHALLENGE: create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer that depi
 cts a bold\, original\, hopeful vision of progress. PRIZES: USD 3.5 millio
 n-plus total\; the grand prize winner gets USD 2.6 million-plus to turn th
 eir trailer into a feature film\, plus over USD 1 million in prizes for ru
 nners-up. BACKGROUND: launched by the nonprofit XPRIZE and funded by Peter
  Diamandis\, with Google and Range as partners\; inspired by the optimism 
 of Star Trek and intended to give storytellers a hopeful 'north star' for 
 builders. ELIGIBILITY: open to all filmmakers globally. TIMELINE: competit
 ion launched 9 March 2026\; submission deadline 15 August 2026\; finals on
  25 September 2026 in Los Angeles (finalists attend in person). APPLY: reg
 ister and read the rules on the contest website at futurevisionxprize.com.
 \n\nOrganisation: XPRIZE (Future Vision XPRIZE\, funded by Peter Diamandis
 \; partners Google and Range)\nLocation: Online / Worldwide (finals held i
 n Los Angeles)\nAward: USD 3.5 million-plus prize pool. Grand prize winner
  receives USD 2.6 million-plus to develop their vision into a feature film
 \, with over USD 1 million in additional prizes for runners-up.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer\n\nMore: https://f
 uturevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://futurevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online / Worldwide (finals held in Los Angeles)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aesthetica-art-prize-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205350Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Deadline: Aesthetica Art Prize 2026 (20th edition)
DESCRIPTION:The Aesthetica Art Prize accepts work in any discipline and the
 me\, with video\, installation\, digital\, and photography regularly short
 listed\; past shortlists frequently feature critical-tech and surveillance
 -adjacent work\, making it a strong venue for media art. Main Prize GBP 10
 \,000 plus a group exhibition at York Art Gallery and editorial coverage. 
 Standard deadline 11 October 2026 (GBP 25 for two works)\; late entries 12
 -18 October 2026 (GBP 35).\n\nOrganisation: Aesthetica Magazine\nLocation:
  York\, United Kingdom (exhibition at York Art Gallery\, spring 2027). Ope
 n worldwide\, no age or nationality restrictions.\nAward: Main Prize GBP 1
 0\,000 plus exhibition at York Art Gallery and publication in the Antholog
 y\; Emerging Prize GBP 1\,000 (students and graduates within 3 years). Ent
 ry GBP 25 for two works (late entries GBP 35).\nDuration: Exhibition at Yo
 rk Art Gallery\, spring 2027.\n\nMore: https://aestheticamagazine.com/artp
 rize/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://aestheticamagazine.com/artprize/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:York\, United Kingdom (exhibition at York Art Gallery\, spring 202
 7). Open worldwide\, no age or nationality restrictions.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondation-schneider-contemporary-talents-earth-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T205350Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260824
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondation Francois Schneider: Contemporary Talents Compet
 ition - The Earth
DESCRIPTION:The Fondation Francois Schneider's Contemporary Talents competi
 tion\, themed The Earth for this edition\, awards EUR 15\,000 per laureate
  (including acquisition of the work\; EUR 8\,000 for editioned works) plus
  an exhibition at the foundation's centre in Wattwiller. ELIGIBILITY: prof
 essional artists internationally\, in SCULPTURE AND INSTALLATION only (vid
 eo or digital work alone does not qualify). NOTE: the 23 August 2026 deadl
 ine is from a listing site\; the organizer page only states the call runs 
 June to August\, so verify the exact date before applying.\n\nOrganisation
 : Fondation Francois Schneider\nLocation: Wattwiller\, France. Open intern
 ationally to professional artists\; sculpture and installation only.\nAwar
 d: EUR 15\,000 per laureate (includes acquisition\; EUR 8\,000 for edition
 ed works)\, plus exhibition at the foundation. No entry fee.\nDuration: Ca
 ll runs June to August 2026\; laureates exhibited at the foundation in Wat
 twiller.\n\nMore: https://www.fondationfrancoisschneider.org/en/contempora
 ry-talents-competition/contemporary-talents-competition-the-earth/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fondationfrancoisschneider.org/en/contemporary-talents-comp
 etition/contemporary-talents-competition-the-earth/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wattwiller\, France. Open internationally to professional artists\
 ; sculpture and installation only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:artist-grant-unrestricted-1200-november-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T205350Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Artist Grant: Unrestricted $1\,200 Visual Artist Grant (N
 ovember 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Artist Grant awards an unrestricted USD 1\,200 grant to one vis
 ual artist three times a year\, on a deliberately low-friction application
 : NO grant proposal is required. You email a link to your website\, or 3-5
  images of your work as JPG\, PNG or PDF\, plus a resume\, CV or short bio
  with your name\, to submit@artistgrant.org\, and separately pay the USD 3
 0 fee through Stripe or PayPal. If the name on your payment differs from t
 he name on your email\, say so in the email. ELIGIBILITY: visual artists a
 ged 18 or over\, worldwide. Past winners may NOT apply again. MEDIA ACCEPT
 ED: painting\, drawing\, sculpture\, ceramics\, printmaking\, photography\
 , mixed media\, installation\, and new or alternative visual art forms. NO
 T ACCEPTED: film and video\, music\, theatre\, dance. SELECTION CRITERIA: 
 a cohesive body of work\; well-crafted work\; well-presented work\, judged
  with an explicit allowance that artists have differing financial means fo
 r presentation\; work that communicates its viewpoint\, ideas and concepts
  clearly\, effectively and creatively\; and work that is not derivative. R
 ESULTS: all applicants are notified within 6-8 weeks of each deadline\, an
 d results are announced on the website\, social media and newsletter. They
  will not respond to individual queries during the review period. VISIBILI
 TY: grantees are showcased on the website\, social media and marketing mat
 erials\, and selected applicants are featured on social media with permiss
 ion. Artists retain their copyrights. NOTE: the grant recurs on 15 March\,
  15 July and 15 November each year\, and this desk lists each round separa
 tely. There is a USD 30 application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Artist Grant\nLo
 cation: Remote (worldwide). No residency or travel component.\nAward: Unre
 stricted USD 1\,200 grant to one visual artist per round\, awarded three t
 imes a year. Application fee of USD 30\, paid separately via Stripe or Pay
 Pal.\nDuration: One-off unrestricted award\; no reporting or project perio
 d\n\nMore: https://artistgrant.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artistgrant.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (worldwide). No residency or travel component.
END:VEVENT
